=begin
      author: Fizzleworth (fork of undead_bounty.lic)
    co-writer: Claude (Anthropic)
        name: bounty_chooser
        game: gemstone
        tags: bounty, adventurer's guild
    requires: Lich > 5.4.0
     version: 1.2

  undead_bounty.lic with the "must be undead" test replaced by an allowed list, and
  with heirloom and rescue-child tasks accepted by AREA.

  Automates the "reroll until it's one I'm hunting" bounty loop:
    1. Go to the Adventurer's Guild and ask the bounty master for a task. With a
       Bounty Boost it asks for a specific type (`ask taskmaster for bounty kill`);
       WITHOUT one (out of boosts) it asks generically and takes whatever is offered,
       and the offer is judged on every type below, not just the one you named.
    2. A creature problem, a lost heirloom or a missing child is followed to the town
       guard, who says which creature and which area; a gem order is followed to that
       town's gem dealer. (Herb/skin/escort/bandit tasks are removed.)
    3. Keep it if it qualifies, otherwise `ask taskmaster for removal` and loop:
         kill ("suppress X activity") and dangerous-creature tasks: the creature's name
           contains anything on your creature list
         heirloom and rescue-child tasks: the task's AREA contains anything on your
           areas list (the attacking creature can be anything)
         gem orders: any gem (they drop while hunting anywhere); optionally only from
           certain towns' dealers (`gem_towns:` in the yaml, empty = any town)

  usage:
    ;bounty_chooser help
    ;bounty_chooser kill skeletal ice troll, cold guardian, frost giant --areas=Ice Plains, Icemule Trail
    ;bounty_chooser dangerous frost giant
    ;bounty_chooser kill            (creatures and areas from data/GSIV/<char>/bounty_chooser.yaml)

  Everything else is inherited: turning in a completed bounty first, leaving an
  acceptable in-progress bounty alone (and any task that is already mid-way, like a
  found heirloom or a made contact with the child), the zero-boost path (exits cleanly
  on the taskmaster's cooldown), the 25-reroll cap, and walking back to the room you
  started in. See undead_bounty.lic for those details.

  changelog:
    1.2
      - accept gem orders (:gem_assignment -> the town's gem dealer -> :gem), optionally
        limited to certain towns with gem_towns
      - the allowed lists travel as one Rules struct (creatures, areas, gem_towns)
    1.1
      - accept :heirloom and :rescue tasks (followed via their assignments) when their
        area is on the areas list; follow heirloom/rescue assignments to the guard
      - mid-task states (found heirloom, child contact, spawned dangerous creature) are
        never tossed for a reroll
    1.0
      - fork of undead_bounty 1.11: creature filter (single partial name, must be
        undead) replaced by a comma-separated allowed list of any creatures

=end

module BountyChooser
  BOUNTY_TYPES = %w[kill dangerous].freeze
  BOUNTY_MASTER_NAME = 'taskmaster'.freeze
  GUARD_NAME_PATTERN = /(?:guard|sergeant|guardsman|sentry|tavernkeeper|alchemist|purser)/i.freeze
  GUARD_NOT_READY_PATTERN = /is in no condition to talk to you/i.freeze

  # debug aid: print every bounty the script received this run, on exit.
  # on for now while we're still shaking bugs out.
  LOG_BOUNTY_HISTORY = true

  def self.bounty_history
    @bounty_history ||= []
  end

  # How many of the creature the bounty wants, or nil when the task doesn't
  # carry a count (e.g. a single named dangerous creature, rescue, heirloom).
  # Bounty::Task has no real #number method -- it only answers through
  # method_missing when requirements has a :number key, and RAISES
  # NoMethodError otherwise, so a plain `task.number || '?'` can never reach
  # its '?' fallback. That crashed the script right after a guard assignment
  # with no count (Picko, 2026-10-20 01:34: "undefined method 'number' for an
  # instance of Lich::Gemstone::Bounty::Task"). Read the hash directly.
  def self.task_number(task)
    task.requirements&.[](:number)
  end

  def self.record_bounty(creature:, number:, type:, location:, verdict:)
    bounty_history << {
      creature: creature,
      number: number,
      type: type,
      location: location,
      verdict: verdict
    }
  end

  def self.print_bounty_history
    return unless LOG_BOUNTY_HISTORY
    return if bounty_history.empty?

    respond ''
    respond "BountyChooser: bounty history for this run (#{bounty_history.length}):"
    bounty_history.each_with_index do |entry, i|
      respond format(
        '  %<n>2d. %<count>3s x %<creature>-24s [%<type>s] near %<location>-20s - %<verdict>s',
        n: i + 1,
        count: entry[:number] || '?',
        creature: entry[:creature] || 'unknown',
        type: entry[:type] || '?',
        location: entry[:location] || '?',
        verdict: entry[:verdict]
      )
    end
  end

  def self.find_npc(pattern)
    (GameObj.npcs.to_a + GameObj.room_desc.to_a).find { |n| n.status != 'dead' && n.name =~ pattern }
  end

  # tries the current room only; returns nil (does not exit) if not found,
  # so callers can move on and try another room
  def self.find_npc_in_room(pattern, retries: 6, delay: 0.25)
    retries.times do
      npc = find_npc(pattern)
      return npc if npc

      sleep delay
    end
    nil
  end

  def self.wait_for_npc(pattern, label)
    npc = find_npc_in_room(pattern, retries: 10)
    if npc.nil?
      respond "BountyChooser: couldn't find #{label} in this room, stopping."
      exit
    end
    npc
  end

  def self.wait_for_bounty
    30.times do |i|
      task = Bounty.current
      return task if task && yield(task)

      sleep 0.25
    end
    nil
  end

  # explicitly asks the game for current bounty status instead of trusting
  # whatever XMLData.bounty_task was last left at (could be stale/unset at
  # the start of a fresh script run)
  def self.refresh_bounty_status
    fput 'bounty'
    waitrt?
    wait_for_bounty { true }
  end

  # matches both "...eligible for new task assignment in about 43 minutes"
  # (from `bounty` status) and "...come back in about 37 minutes if you
  # want another task" (from asking the taskmaster while on cooldown)
  MINUTES_PATTERN = /in about (\d+) minutes?/i.freeze

  def self.minutes_until_eligible(text)
    m = MINUTES_PATTERN.match(text.to_s)
    m && m[1].to_i
  end

  # sends a command once (no auto-resend) and watches incoming lines for up
  # to `timeout` seconds for any of the given patterns; returns the matching
  # pattern, or nil if none showed up in time
  # returns the matching pattern (not the line) to keep existing `matched
  # == SOME_PATTERN` call sites simple; the actual matched line is stashed
  # in @last_matched_line for the rare caller (e.g. minute-count parsing)
  # that needs the real text.
  def self.fput_and_check(command, patterns, timeout: 5)
    Script.current.clear
    fput command
    end_time = Time.now + timeout
    while Time.now < end_time
      line = get?
      if line.nil?
        sleep 0.1
      elsif (pattern = patterns.find { |p| line =~ p })
        @last_matched_line = line
        return pattern
      end
    end
    nil
  end

  # polls npc.status (mutated in place by Lich as server updates arrive)
  # until it's no longer sleeping, or timeout is hit
  def self.wait_for_npc_awake(npc, timeout: 120)
    return unless npc.status.to_s =~ /sleep/i

    respond 'BountyChooser: guard is sleeping, waiting for them to wake up...'
    end_time = Time.now + timeout
    while Time.now < end_time && npc.status.to_s =~ /sleep/i
      sleep 1
    end
  end

  # find the town's guard room(s) generically: any room tagged 'advguard' (or
  # 'advguard2') whose nearest 'town'-tagged room matches the given town
  # name, sorted closest-to-current-position first. Some towns have more
  # than one (e.g. Wehnimer's Landing has the gate guard AND a guard inside
  # Helga's Tavern), so callers should try each in turn.
  def self.resolve_guard_rooms(town_name)
    return [] if town_name.to_s.empty?

    town_room = Room.list.find { |r| r.tags.include?('town') && r.location.to_s.include?(town_name) }
    return [] unless town_room

    candidates = Room.list.find_all do |r|
      r.tags.any? { |t| t =~ /^advguard/ } && r.find_nearest_by_tag('town') == town_room.id
    end
    return [] if candidates.empty?

    candidates.map(&:id).sort_by { |id| Room.current.path_to(id)&.length || Float::INFINITY }
  end

  # Rooms in the given town tagged 'gemshop', closest first -- where the gem dealer is.
  def self.resolve_gemshop_rooms(town_name)
    return [] if town_name.to_s.empty?

    town_room = Room.list.find { |r| r.tags.include?('town') && r.location.to_s.include?(town_name) }
    return [] unless town_room

    candidates = Room.list.find_all do |r|
      r.tags.include?('gemshop') && r.find_nearest_by_tag('town') == town_room.id
    end
    candidates.map(&:id).sort_by { |id| Room.current.path_to(id)&.length || Float::INFINITY }
  end

  # A gem assignment names the town and the dealer ("The local gem dealer, Zirconia, has
  # an order to fill ..."): walk to that town's gem shop, find the dealer, and ASK about
  # bounties to get the actual order (:gem task: gem, number, town).
  def self.ask_dealer_for_bounty(assignment)
    town = assignment.town
    name_hint = assignment.requirements[:npc_name].to_s.split.first
    pattern = Regexp.union(*[name_hint, 'gem dealer', 'gemcutter'].compact.reject(&:empty?).map { |n| /#{Regexp.escape(n)}/i })

    npc = nil
    resolve_gemshop_rooms(town).each do |room_id|
      Script.run('go2', room_id.to_s)
      waitrt?
      npc = find_npc_in_room(pattern)
      break if npc

      respond "BountyChooser: no gem dealer at room #{room_id}, trying the next location..."
    end
    unless npc
      respond "BountyChooser: couldn't find the gem dealer in '#{town}', stopping."
      exit
    end

    task = nil
    6.times do
      fput "ask #{npc.noun} about bounty"
      waitrt?
      task = wait_for_bounty(&:ready?)
      break if task
    end
    unless task
      respond 'BountyChooser: the gem dealer never gave a gem order, stopping.'
      exit
    end
    task
  end

  def self.go_to_advguild
    Script.run('go2', 'advguild')
    waitrt?
  end

  # returns true if a Bounty Boost is active (already was, or "boost bounty"
  # just activated one); false if there are none to redeem - in that case
  # we still go ahead and ask the taskmaster, since F2P accounts sometimes
  # have a free task available even with zero boosts (it's the "eligible
  # for new task assignment in about N minutes" cooldown that gates that,
  # not the boost itself).
  def self.boost_bounty
    if Effects::Buffs.active?('Bounty Boost')
      respond 'BountyChooser: Bounty Boost already active, skipping "boost bounty".'
      return true
    end

    result = dothistimeout('boost bounty', 5, /You do not have any Bounty Boosts to redeem\.|You have activated a Bounty Boost\./)
    waitrt?

    if result =~ /You do not have any Bounty Boosts to redeem/
      respond "BountyChooser: #{result} Trying the taskmaster anyway in case a free task is available."
      return false
    end

    # the Buffs dialog data lags a bit behind the chat confirmation, so give
    # it a few seconds to catch up before treating it as a real failure
    active = false
    12.times do
      active = Effects::Buffs.active?('Bounty Boost')
      break if active

      sleep 0.5
    end

    unless active
      respond 'BountyChooser: Bounty Boost does not appear to be active after "boost bounty", stopping.'
      exit
    end

    true
  end

  ALREADY_ASSIGNED_PATTERN = /already been assigned a task/i.freeze
  TASKMASTER_BUSY_PATTERN = /kind of busy right now/i.freeze
  NO_SUITABLE_TASK_PATTERN = /don't seem to have any tasks that are suitable for you/i.freeze
  # this reuses the same opening line as TASKMASTER_BUSY_PATTERN, but with a
  # real multi-minute cooldown attached - only seen (so far) when asking
  # without a Bounty Boost active
  TASKMASTER_COOLDOWN_PATTERN = /come back in about .+ if you want another task/i.freeze

  # Task#assigned? matches ANY "...assignment" type - herb_assignment,
  # gem_assignment, skin_assignment, heirloom_assignment, rescue_assignment,
  # bandit_assignment, creature_assignment. This script only knows how to
  # follow the creature_assignment ("It appears they have a creature
  # problem they'd like you to solve") track through the town guard to a
  # cull/dangerous task. Any other assignment type sent to ask_guard_for_bounty
  # just has the guard saying "I don't have any tasks for you right now" in
  # an endless-looking loop, since that quest was never routed through them.
  def self.creature_assignment?(task)
    task&.type == :creature_assignment
  end

  # What this fork follows: a creature problem (-> :cull / :dangerous), a lost heirloom
  # (-> :heirloom) or a missing child (-> :rescue) via the town guard, and a gem order
  # (-> :gem) via the town's gem dealer. The latter two
  # carry the attacking creature and an area, like the cull tasks do. Everything
  # else (herb/gem/skin/escort/bandit) is still removed.
  FOLLOWED_ASSIGNMENTS = %i[creature_assignment heirloom_assignment rescue_assignment gem_assignment].freeze

  def self.follow_assignment?(task)
    FOLLOWED_ASSIGNMENTS.include?(task&.type)
  end

  # Task types worth taking when the AREA is right, whatever the creature (heirloom
  # and rescue tasks send you after one specific attacker in a specific area).
  AREA_TASK_TYPES = %i[heirloom rescue].freeze
  # Mid-task states with too little data to judge (no creature/area in the text): never
  # tossed for a reroll.
  IN_PROGRESS_STATES = %i[dangerous_spawned heirloom_found rescue_spawned].freeze

  # What counts as a good task. creatures/areas/gem_towns are lowercase lists.
  Rules = Struct.new(:creatures, :areas, :gem_towns)

  def self.ask_master_for_bounty(bounty_type, max_attempts: 10)
    go_to_advguild

    # asking for a SPECIFIC bounty type requires an active Bounty Boost -
    # without one, the game doesn't support it at all, so don't even try
    return ask_master_for_free_bounty unless boost_bounty

    max_attempts.times do
      matched = fput_and_check(
        "ask #{BOUNTY_MASTER_NAME} for bounty #{bounty_type}",
        [ALREADY_ASSIGNED_PATTERN, TASKMASTER_BUSY_PATTERN, NO_SUITABLE_TASK_PATTERN]
      )
      waitrt?

      if matched == NO_SUITABLE_TASK_PATTERN
        respond "BountyChooser: taskmaster has no #{bounty_type} tasks suitable for you here - this hunting"
        respond 'ground has probably become too easy for your level. Try another town, or a different'
        respond 'bounty type, stopping.'
        exit
      elsif matched == ALREADY_ASSIGNED_PATTERN
        respond 'BountyChooser: taskmaster says a task is already assigned, requesting removal...'
        ask_master_for_removal
        next
      elsif matched == TASKMASTER_BUSY_PATTERN
        respond 'BountyChooser: taskmaster is busy, retrying in 3 seconds...'
        sleep 3
        next
      end

      # Task#assigned? only matches types ending in "assignment" - but some
      # types (e.g. :escort) get handed out directly in their final "ready"
      # form, skipping that intermediate stage entirely, so they'd go
      # unrecognized here and only get cleaned up later (if at all) via the
      # "already assigned" text fallback above. any? (anything but :none)
      # catches both shapes.
      task = wait_for_bounty(&:any?)
      next unless task

      if follow_assignment?(task)
        return task
      end

      respond "BountyChooser: taskmaster assigned a #{task.type} task (not a creature, heirloom or rescue problem), " \
              'requesting removal and retrying...'
      ask_master_for_removal
    end

    respond 'BountyChooser: never got a new creature-problem assignment from the bounty master, stopping.'
    exit
  end

  # no Bounty Boost active: can't request a specific type, so just ask
  # generically and take whatever's offered. Unlike the boosted path, there's
  # no point retrying here if it's not a creature problem - without a boost
  # a fresh assignment is a real cooldown away, so just remove it and stop.
  def self.ask_master_for_free_bounty
    2.times do
      matched = fput_and_check(
        "ask #{BOUNTY_MASTER_NAME} about bounty",
        [ALREADY_ASSIGNED_PATTERN, TASKMASTER_COOLDOWN_PATTERN]
      )
      waitrt?

      if matched == ALREADY_ASSIGNED_PATTERN
        respond 'BountyChooser: taskmaster says a task is already assigned, requesting removal...'
        ask_master_for_removal
        next
      elsif matched == TASKMASTER_COOLDOWN_PATTERN
        @eligible_in_minutes = minutes_until_eligible(@last_matched_line) || @eligible_in_minutes
        wait_note = @eligible_in_minutes ? " (eligible again in about #{@eligible_in_minutes} minutes)" : ''
        respond "BountyChooser: no Bounty Boost available and no free task assignment right now#{wait_note}."
        respond 'BountyChooser: nothing to do - stopping so the hunt/rest cycle can just try again later.'
        exit
      end

      # Task#assigned? only matches types ending in "assignment" - but some
      # types (e.g. :escort) get handed out directly in their final "ready"
      # form, skipping that intermediate stage entirely, so they'd go
      # unrecognized here and only get cleaned up later (if at all) via the
      # "already assigned" text fallback above. any? (anything but :none)
      # catches both shapes.
      task = wait_for_bounty(&:any?)
      next unless task

      return task if follow_assignment?(task)

      respond "BountyChooser: no Bounty Boost, and the free task offered was a #{task.type} task, not a " \
              "creature, heirloom or rescue problem. Removing it and stopping so the hunt/rest cycle can try again later."
      ask_master_for_removal
      exit
    end

    respond 'BountyChooser: no Bounty Boost, and the taskmaster never confirmed a task or a cooldown - stopping.'
    exit
  end

  def self.ask_master_for_removal
    go_to_advguild
    2.times do
      fput "ask #{BOUNTY_MASTER_NAME} for removal"
      waitrt?
    end
  end

  GUARD_TASK_COMPLETE_PATTERN = /successfully completed your task/i.freeze
  TASKMASTER_TURN_IN_PATTERN = /Good job/i.freeze

  # if a previous run already finished killing/gathering/etc. and just never
  # got turned in, `bounty` reports "You succeeded in your task and should
  # report back to..." (Bounty.current.type == :guard). Handle that before
  # starting a new reroll loop: report to the guard, then the taskmaster,
  # then bank the reward.
  def self.turn_in_bounty(task)
    respond 'BountyChooser: found a completed bounty waiting to be turned in, handling that first...'

    npc = locate_guard(task.town)
    confirmed = false
    5.times do
      wait_for_npc_awake(npc)
      matched = fput_and_check("ask #{npc.noun} about bounty", [GUARD_TASK_COMPLETE_PATTERN, GUARD_NOT_READY_PATTERN])
      waitrt?

      if matched == GUARD_NOT_READY_PATTERN
        respond "BountyChooser: #{npc.noun} isn't able to talk right now, waiting and retrying..."
        sleep 5
        next
      end

      confirmed = !matched.nil?
      break
    end

    unless confirmed
      respond "BountyChooser: #{npc.noun} didn't confirm the completed task, stopping so you can check manually."
      exit
    end

    go_to_advguild
    confirmed = false
    5.times do
      matched = fput_and_check("ask #{BOUNTY_MASTER_NAME} about bounty", [TASKMASTER_TURN_IN_PATTERN, TASKMASTER_BUSY_PATTERN])
      waitrt?

      if matched == TASKMASTER_BUSY_PATTERN
        respond 'BountyChooser: taskmaster is busy, retrying in 3 seconds...'
        sleep 3
        next
      end

      confirmed = !matched.nil?
      break
    end

    unless confirmed
      respond 'BountyChooser: taskmaster never confirmed the turn-in, stopping so you can check manually.'
      exit
    end

    respond 'BountyChooser: bounty turned in, depositing at the bank...'
    Script.run('go2', 'bank')
    waitrt?
    fput 'deposit all'
    waitrt?
  end

  # checks status ONCE before touching anything, and handles whatever's
  # already there:
  #   - a completed task waiting on a guard report -> turn it in
  #   - an in-progress task that already qualifies (its creature is on the
  #     allowed list) -> leave it alone, don't burn it on a reroll
  #   - anything else (:none, or an in-progress task that doesn't qualify)
  #     -> nothing to do here, let the normal reroll loop handle it
  # returns :already_matching if the in-progress bounty already qualifies,
  # so run() knows to stop instead of starting the reroll loop.
  def self.handle_existing_bounty(rules)
    task = refresh_bounty_status
    return unless task

    if task.type == :guard
      turn_in_bounty(task)
      return
    end

    # :none can still carry a "You will be eligible for new task assignment
    # in about N minutes" cooldown notice - stash it so a later "couldn't
    # get a task" exit message can mention it instead of just failing blind.
    # NOTE: Task#description is never actually populated by the parser, so
    # we have to go back to the raw bounty stream text via checkbounty.
    @eligible_in_minutes = minutes_until_eligible(checkbounty) if task.type == :none

    if IN_PROGRESS_STATES.include?(task.type)
      record_bounty(creature: task.creature, number: task_number(task), type: task.type, location: task.location,
                    verdict: 'mid-task - left as-is')
      respond "BountyChooser: you're partway through a #{task.type} task - leaving it alone."
      return :already_matching
    end

    return unless task.creature || task.type == :gem
    return unless task_acceptable?(task, rules)

    creature = task.creature
    record_bounty(creature: creature, number: task_number(task), type: task.type, location: task.location,
                  verdict: 'ALLOWED - already in progress, left as-is')
    respond "BountyChooser: current bounty is already #{describe_task(task)} - acceptable, leaving it alone."
    :already_matching
  end

  # remembers which guard room actually had the guard, per town, so later
  # loop iterations don't have to re-check every candidate room every time
  def self.guard_room_cache
    @guard_room_cache ||= {}
  end

  # travels to the given town's guard room(s) (using the cache, then the
  # generic tag-based search, same as before) and returns the guard npc.
  # exits if no guard can be found anywhere.
  def self.locate_guard(town)
    npc = nil
    found_room = nil
    cached_room = guard_room_cache[town]

    if cached_room
      Script.run('go2', cached_room.to_s)
      waitrt?
      npc = find_npc_in_room(GUARD_NAME_PATTERN)
      found_room = cached_room if npc
    end

    unless npc
      room_ids = resolve_guard_rooms(town)
      if room_ids.empty?
        respond "BountyChooser: couldn't find a guard room for '#{town}', falling back to the nearest advguard tag."
        room_ids = ['advguard']
      end

      room_ids.each do |room_id|
        next if room_id == cached_room # already tried above

        Script.run('go2', room_id.to_s)
        waitrt?
        npc = find_npc_in_room(GUARD_NAME_PATTERN)
        if npc
          found_room = room_id
          break
        end

        respond "BountyChooser: no guard found at room #{room_id}, trying the next location..."
      end
    end

    unless npc
      respond "BountyChooser: couldn't find the town guard at any known location for '#{town}', stopping."
      exit
    end

    # only cache real room ids, not the 'advguard' tag fallback
    guard_room_cache[town] = found_room if found_room.is_a?(Integer)
    npc
  end

  def self.ask_guard_for_bounty(assignment)
    npc = locate_guard(assignment.town)

    task = nil
    10.times do
      wait_for_npc_awake(npc)

      matched = fput_and_check("ask #{npc.noun} for bounty", [GUARD_NOT_READY_PATTERN])
      waitrt?

      if matched
        respond "BountyChooser: #{npc.noun} isn't able to talk right now, waiting and retrying..."
        sleep 5
        next
      end

      task = wait_for_bounty(&:ready?)
      break if task
    end

    unless task
      respond "BountyChooser: guard never gave a creature assignment, stopping."
      exit
    end
    task
  end

  # each type's 'name' pattern is one big regex: ^(?:adjective prefixes)?(name1|name2|...)$
  # pull the literal creature names out of the middle group so we can search
  # them, rather than matching against it directly.
  def self.creature_names_from_pattern(pattern)
    source = pattern&.source.to_s
    return [] if source.empty?

    boundary = source.index(')?(')
    body = boundary ? source[(boundary + 3)..-1] : source
    body = body.sub(/\)\$\z/, '')

    body.split('|').map { |n| n.delete('\\') }.reject(&:empty?)
  end

  # every creature name gameobj-data.xml knows about, across every type - used only
  # to catch typos in the allowed list before a Bounty Boost gets spent.
  def self.known_creatures
    return @known_creatures if defined?(@known_creatures)

    GameObj.load_data if GameObj.type_data.nil? || GameObj.type_data.empty?
    names = []
    GameObj.type_data.each_value { |fields| names.concat(creature_names_from_pattern(fields[:name])) }
    @known_creatures = names.uniq
  end

  # partial, case-insensitive search against every known creature name
  def self.find_creature_matches(query)
    return [] if query.to_s.strip.empty?

    q = query.strip.downcase
    known_creatures.select { |name| name.downcase.include?(q) }
  end

  # The allowed list: a task's creature qualifies if its name contains any entry
  # (case-insensitive), e.g. "skeletal ice troll" for a "skeletal ice troll" bounty.
  def self.creature_allowed?(creature_name, creatures)
    name = creature_name.to_s.downcase
    return false if name.empty?

    creatures.any? { |entry| !entry.empty? && name.include?(entry.downcase) }
  end

  # The area of a task ("Ice Plains", "Icemule Trail"), matched like creatures are.
  def self.area_allowed?(area, areas)
    name = area.to_s.downcase
    return false if name.empty?

    areas.any? { |entry| !entry.empty? && name.include?(entry.downcase) }
  end

  # Gem orders: any gem is fine (they drop while hunting anywhere); only the TOWN of the
  # dealer matters, because that's where it has to be turned in. No gem_towns = any town.
  def self.gem_town_allowed?(town, gem_towns)
    return true if gem_towns.empty?

    name = town.to_s.downcase
    !name.empty? && gem_towns.any? { |entry| !entry.empty? && name.include?(entry.downcase) }
  end

  # Is this task one to keep?
  #   kill / dangerous-creature tasks (:cull, :dangerous): the creature is on the list
  #   heirloom / rescue-child tasks: the AREA is on the areas list (the creature can be
  #     anything -- these are about being in the right place)
  #   gem orders (:gem): any gem; the dealer's town must be allowed (if gem_towns is set)
  def self.task_acceptable?(task, rules)
    case task.type
    when :cull, :dangerous
      creature_allowed?(task.creature, rules.creatures)
    when *AREA_TASK_TYPES
      area_allowed?(task.location, rules.areas)
    when :gem
      gem_town_allowed?(task.town, rules.gem_towns)
    else
      false
    end
  end

  def self.describe_task(task)
    case task.type
    when *AREA_TASK_TYPES
      "#{task.type} task (attacker: #{task.creature || '?'}) in/near #{task.location}"
    when :gem
      "gem order: #{task_number(task) || '?'} x #{task.requirements[:gem] || 'gems'} for #{task.requirements[:npc_name] || 'the dealer'} in #{task.town || '?'}"
    else
      "#{task_number(task) || '?'} x #{task.creature} [#{task.type}] in/near #{task.location}"
    end
  end

  # max rerolls before giving up - guards against an endless loop if the
  # creature name has a typo, or it's a bounty that just can't be assigned
  # (e.g. wrong level range)
  MAX_ATTEMPTS = 25

  def self.run(bounty_type, rules)
    # module-level state survives across separate script runs in the same
    # Lich session, so reset it at the start of each run
    @bounty_history = []
    @eligible_in_minutes = nil
    start_room = Room.current.id

    return if handle_existing_bounty(rules) == :already_matching

    attempt = 0

    loop do
      attempt += 1
      if attempt > MAX_ATTEMPTS
        respond "BountyChooser: hit the #{MAX_ATTEMPTS}-attempt limit without landing on a match, stopping."
        respond 'BountyChooser: double check the creature names/spelling, or these bounties may not be assignable at your level.'
        return
      end

      assignment = ask_master_for_bounty(bounty_type)

      # A gem order in a town you don't want is removed before walking there.
      if assignment.type == :gem_assignment && !gem_town_allowed?(assignment.town, rules.gem_towns)
        record_bounty(creature: nil, number: nil, type: assignment.type, location: assignment.town,
                      verdict: 'gem order in an unwanted town - rerolled')
        respond "BountyChooser: gem order in #{assignment.town}, not one of #{rules.gem_towns.join(', ')} - requesting removal and rerolling..."
        ask_master_for_removal
        next
      end

      task = assignment.type == :gem_assignment ? ask_dealer_for_bounty(assignment) : ask_guard_for_bounty(assignment)

      unless task.creature || task.type == :gem
        record_bounty(creature: nil, number: task_number(task), type: task.type, location: task.location,
                       verdict: "couldn't parse creature from guard response")
        respond "BountyChooser: could not determine the bounty creature from the guard's response, stopping."
        return
      end

      creature = task.creature
      respond "BountyChooser: assigned #{describe_task(task)}."

      if task_acceptable?(task, rules)
        record_bounty(creature: creature, number: task_number(task), type: task.type, location: task.location,
                       verdict: 'ALLOWED - stopped here')
        respond "BountyChooser: that one qualifies - stopping, take it from here."
        return
      end

      record_bounty(creature: creature, number: task_number(task), type: task.type, location: task.location,
                    verdict: 'not on the allowed list - rerolled')

      respond "BountyChooser: that one doesn't qualify, requesting removal and rerolling..."
      ask_master_for_removal
    end
  ensure
    print_bounty_history
    return_to_room(start_room)
  end

  def self.return_to_room(room_id)
    return if room_id.nil? || Room.current.id == room_id

    respond "BountyChooser: heading back to your starting room (#{room_id})..."
    Script.run('go2', room_id.to_s)
    waitrt?
  end

  def self.show_help
    n = Script.current.name
    respond 'usage:'
    respond "    ;#{n} help"
    respond "    ;#{n} kill skeletal ice troll, cold guardian, frost giant --areas=Ice Plains, Icemule Trail"
    respond "    ;#{n} dangerous frost giant"
    respond "    ;#{n} kill            - no list given: use data/GSIV/<char>/bounty_chooser.yaml"
    respond ''
    respond 'Kill ("suppress X activity") and dangerous-creature bounties are kept when the'
    respond 'creature name CONTAINS any entry of the (comma-separated) creature list, case-'
    respond 'insensitive. The creature does NOT have to be undead. Heirloom and rescue-child'
    respond 'bounties are kept when their AREA contains any entry of --areas= (the attacker can'
    respond 'be anything); with no areas listed they are removed. Gem orders are kept too (any'
    respond 'gem; optionally only for certain towns -- see gem_towns below).'
    respond ''
    respond 'The yaml file looks like:'
    respond '    creatures:'
    respond '      - skeletal ice troll'
    respond '      - cold guardian'
    respond '      - frost giant'
    respond '    areas:'
    respond '      - Ice Plains'
    respond '      - Icemule Trail'
    respond '    gem_towns:            # optional; leave out for gem orders from any town'
    respond '      - Icemule Trace'
    respond ''
    respond 'Creature names are checked against the known creatures before the script leaves'
    respond 'the guild -- a list where nothing matches is rejected instead of burning a boost.'
    respond ''
    respond 'With a Bounty Boost it asks the taskmaster for the bounty type you name. WITHOUT one'
    respond '(out of boosts) it asks generically and judges whatever it is offered on all of the'
    respond 'rules above; if that is not acceptable it removes it, and the next ask normally hits'
    respond "the taskmaster's cooldown, which ends the run cleanly (try again at the next rest)."
    respond ''
    respond 'Also: a completed bounty is turned in first (guard, taskmaster, bank); an acceptable'
    respond 'in-progress bounty, or one that is partway done, is left alone; rerolls are capped at'
    respond "#{BountyChooser::MAX_ATTEMPTS}; and it walks you back to the room you started in when it ends."
  end
end

## script.vars[0] is the entire raw argument string; the individual
## space-split tokens start at script.vars[1].
if script.vars[1].to_s.strip =~ /^help$/i
  BountyChooser.show_help
  exit
end

bounty_type = (script.vars[1] || 'kill').downcase
unless BountyChooser::BOUNTY_TYPES.include?(bounty_type)
  respond "BountyChooser: unknown bounty type '#{bounty_type}', expected one of: #{BountyChooser::BOUNTY_TYPES.join(', ')}"
  exit
end

# Allowed creatures and areas: from the command line, else the yaml file.
#   ;bounty_chooser kill skeletal ice troll, cold guardian --areas=Ice Plains, Icemule Trail
rest = script.vars[2..-1].to_a.join(' ')
areas_arg = rest[/--areas=(.*)\z/i, 1]
creature_arg = rest.sub(/--areas=.*\z/i, '')
split_list = ->(text) { text.to_s.split(',').map { |c| c.strip.downcase }.reject(&:empty?) }
creatures = split_list.call(creature_arg)
areas = split_list.call(areas_arg)

path = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'bounty_chooser.yaml')
require 'yaml'
saved = (YAML.load_file(path, permitted_classes: [Symbol]) rescue nil)
saved = {} unless saved.is_a?(Hash)
# Towns whose gem dealer you'll take an order from; empty = any town.
gem_towns = Array(saved['gem_towns'] || saved[:gem_towns]).map { |c| c.to_s.strip.downcase }.reject(&:empty?)
if creatures.empty? || areas.empty?
  if creatures.empty?
    creatures = Array(saved['creatures'] || saved[:creatures]).map { |c| c.to_s.strip.downcase }.reject(&:empty?)
    respond "BountyChooser: using the creature list from #{File.basename(path)}." unless creatures.empty?
  end
  if areas.empty?
    areas = Array(saved['areas'] || saved[:areas]).map { |c| c.to_s.strip.downcase }.reject(&:empty?)
  end
end

if creatures.empty?
  respond "BountyChooser: no creature list given and none in #{path} -- try ;#{Script.current.name} help"
  exit
end

# Typo guard, before a Bounty Boost can be spent: every entry that matches no known
# creature is called out, and a list where NOTHING matches is rejected outright.
unknown = creatures.reject { |c| BountyChooser.find_creature_matches(c).any? }
if unknown.length == creatures.length
  respond "BountyChooser: none of #{creatures.map { |c| "'#{c}'" }.join(', ')} match a known creature name -- check the spelling, stopping."
  exit
end
respond "BountyChooser: unrecognised name#{'s' if unknown.length > 1} #{unknown.map { |c| "'#{c}'" }.join(', ')} (will still match by name)." unless unknown.empty?
respond "BountyChooser: accepting kill / dangerous-creature bounties for: #{creatures.join(', ')}"
if areas.empty?
  respond 'BountyChooser: no areas set, so heirloom and rescue-child tasks will be removed (add `areas:` to the yaml to allow them).'
else
  respond "BountyChooser: and heirloom / rescue-child tasks in: #{areas.join(', ')}"
end

respond "BountyChooser: and gem orders#{gem_towns.empty? ? ' in any town' : " from the gem dealers in: #{gem_towns.join(', ')}"}."

BountyChooser.run(bounty_type, BountyChooser::Rules.new(creatures, areas, gem_towns))
